+
+Full-family Fourier filtering averages representations over operand pairs with the same answer. A lookup-table memorizer achieves perfect filtered accuracy despite chance-level held-out predictions. We therefore interpret filtering and rescaling as interventions on a task-informed projection. Raw-feature decoders and adjacent swaps establish surviving information independently of that projection.
 
 \textbf{Contributions.}
 \begin{itemize}\itemsep0pt
-\item \textbf{Phenomenon.} Post-grokking collapse under split-optimizer routing is universal across our Muon sweep and reproduced by AdamW at larger step sizes; training accuracy falls with test, and the optimizers differ in severity, not in kind (\S\ref{sec:speed}).
-\item \textbf{Mechanism.} The failure is localized causally to the representation--readout interface: matched branches from bit-identical states show that freezing either side prevents it, and anchoring the embeddings and readout after circuit formation eliminates it on every seed (\S\ref{sec:localize}).
-\item \textbf{Taxonomy.} Filtering to the task-selected Fourier family separates circuit failure from circuit masking; masking is a competition on amplitude that rescaling alone resolves, and grokking is the same competition resolving upward (\S\ref{sec:outvoted}).
-\item \textbf{Methodology.} Support- and power-based progress measures are invariant to the failure and certify an intact circuit at the step the function dies; functional measures are required to see it (Figure~\ref{fig:collapse}, \S\ref{sec:outvoted}).
+\item \textbf{Acute failure and surviving information.} Adjacent swaps isolate damaging readout updates in five unnormalized trajectories; training-only decoders recover high held-out accuracy, and a feature-mean intervention nearly reproduces each failure (\S\ref{sec:localize}).
+\item \textbf{Numerical mechanism and architectural boundary.} Matched arithmetic corrections test prevention over fixed horizons. Captured updates overshoot accurate local descent directions, and an accurate-loss RMS control fails through its embeddings (\S\ref{sec:arithmetic}).
+\item \textbf{Scope of Fourier evidence.} An averaging identity and memorizer controls delimit the interpretation of full-family filtering and rescaling (\S\ref{sec:family}, \S\ref{sec:outvoted}).
 \end{itemize}
 
 \section{Setup}
 \label{sec:setup}
 
-\textbf{Task.} We train on $(a+b)\bmod p$ with $p=113$ throughout, and on $(a-b)\bmod p$ where stated, on the token sequence $[a,b,=]$ with $113$ output classes. A fixed random $30\%$ of the $p^2$ operand grid is the training set, trained full batch with cross-entropy; evaluation is every $100$ steps.
-
-\textbf{Architecture.} The model is a decoder-only transformer, $d_{\text{model}}=128$, four heads, MLP width $512$, ReLU, sequence length $3$, every projection bias-free, and no normalization layers. The absence of normalization makes the residual stream exactly invariant to an invertible change of basis absorbed by the matrices that write to and read from it; LayerNorm is the one operation that distinguishes a coordinate system there. Gain-free RMS normalization would restrict the symmetry to $O(d)$ rather than remove it. Depth is varied by appending blocks under nested initialization.
