 \section{Construction and alignment separate in depth}
 \label{sec:depth}
 
-Depth grows the speed advantage, from $2.22\times$ at depth 2 to past $5.7\times$ at depth 4, where the AdamW baseline never sustains generalization, and it removes the condition that separated the optimizers: the AdamW configuration stable at depth 1 records $556$ sub-threshold evaluations at depth 2. Stage-level interventions locate the code. Frequency- and phase-specific sensitivity first appears at an MLP activation in ten of eleven solved checkpoints and at no attention write, while every earlier stage is computationally necessary without carrying the code, which is why ablation alone cannot locate a circuit. Decoding a post-block residual directly with the unembedding reaches $95\%$ only at the final block in all $41$ generalizing checkpoints and never exceeds $17.97\%$ earlier: an MLP in the penultimate block writes the code and the final block makes it legible, so adding depth adds stages whose residual states are not aligned with the readout and does not distribute the alignment across them. The interface the collapse runs along does not grow with the model, and anchoring it at depth 4 cuts sub-$90\%$ evaluations twenty-fold on an exact-state matched branch (Appendix~\ref{app:depth}).
