 \section{Related work}
 \label{sec:related}
 
-\textbf{Grokking on modular arithmetic.} \citet{power2022grokking} introduced the phenomenon; \citet{nanda2023progress} reverse-engineered the Fourier algorithm and the progress measures this paper tests, establishing that the circuit forms before the accuracy jump and that the jump is a cleanup phase. \citet{zhong2023clock} show hyperparameters select qualitatively different algorithms; \citet{chughtai2023toy} establish universality across architectures and seeds.
-
-\textbf{Failure after grokking.} \citet{thilak2022slingshot} report cyclic instability under adaptive optimizers; \citet{varma2023explaining} describe ungrokking under reduced data; \citet{prieto2025grokking} identify softmax collapse and a naive loss-minimization direction that descends by scaling logits; \citet{prakash2025grokking} report an anti-grokking phase in which training accuracy stays perfect. The failure here escapes those measures and is not that phase: training accuracy falls with test in the same interval, and the direction traveled is underdetermined rather than descending.
-
-\textbf{Muon.} \citet{jordan2024muon} introduced the optimizer and \citet{liu2025muon} deployed it at scale under the routing used here; \citet{tveit2025muon} and \citet{wang2026active} report faster grokking, the latter isolating orthogonalization as the cause and five Newton--Schulz iterations as the robust choice over short horizons; the collapse here occurs at those five iterations over longer ones. \citet{ruan2026muon} and \citet{wang2025tailend} report higher effective rank and a more isotropic spectrum under Muon; we measure the same difference in the basis the model computes in and implicate the normalized-orthogonalization path by ablation.
-
-\textbf{Representation and readout.} \citet{elhage2021framework} state the residual stream's basis freedom this paper operationalizes. \citet{anthes2023diagnosing} identify representation--readout misalignment as the largest component of forgetting in continual learning, produced by new tasks; \citet{chou2026twospeeds} and \citet{gomezjurado2026longdelay} decompose the approach to grokking into representation and readout speeds. Here there is no distribution shift and no new task: the training set stays solved while the sides separate, and the dissociation appears on the far side of generalization as well as before it.
+\textbf{Grokking on modular arithmetic.} \citet{power2022grokking} introduced the phenomenon. \citet{nanda2023progress} reverse-engineered a Fourier algorithm, used causal ablations, and introduced restricted and excluded losses to track circuit formation and cleanup. \citet{zhong2023clock} show that hyperparameters select qualitatively different algorithms; \citet{chughtai2023toy} find shared algorithmic structure alongside variation across learned circuits.
+
+\textbf{Failure after grokking.} \citet{thilak2022slingshot} report cyclic instability under adaptive optimizers; \citet{varma2023explaining} describe ungrokking under reduced data; \citet{prieto2025grokking} identify softmax collapse and a loss-minimization direction that scales logits. \citet{liu2026glitching} connect finite-precision class-sum violations to coupled feature/classifier-mean growth, amplified Adam updates, and loss spikes; they test zero-sum corrections and normalization. Our arithmetic controls extend this account under Muon/AdamW routing. Adjacent swaps and the mean-dependent displacement intervention locate acute failures; fresh decoders measure surviving information. Joint train/test collapse differs from the perfect-training regime of anti-grokking \citep{prakash2025grokking}. The accurate-loss RMS control identifies an embedding failure in our normalized setting.
+
+\textbf{Muon.} \citet{jordan2024muon} introduced the optimizer and \citet{liu2025muon} deployed it at scale under the routing used here. \citet{tveit2025muon} and \citet{wang2026active} report faster grokking in their tested settings; the latter studies orthogonalization and the speed/stability tradeoff with iteration count, including accuracy dips. We examine the five-iteration configuration over longer horizons. \citet{ruan2026muon} and \citet{wang2025tailend} report higher effective rank and a more isotropic weight spectrum under Muon. Our Fourier measurements concern dispersion over operand frequencies, and the joint ablation tests the contribution of normalization and orthogonalization.
+
+\textbf{Representation and readout.} \citet{elhage2021framework} describe residual-stream basis freedom. \citet{anthes2023diagnosing} identify readout misalignment as a major component of forgetting under new tasks. \citet{chou2026twospeeds} use same-split linear probes to diagnose readout miscalibration during grokking and study relative representation and readout learning speeds, while \citet{gomezjurado2026longdelay} finds a decoder bottleneck in one-step Collatz prediction. Here the task stays fixed and the dissociation occurs after generalization: joint train/test failure can coexist with high accuracy under a fresh decoder.
 
 \section{Discussion}
 \label{sec:discussion}
 
-The account is stated at the level of the symmetry that produces it: the residual basis freedom is exact over $GL(d)$ here and restricted to $O(d)$ under gain-free RMS normalization; the drift we measure preserves the family's power distribution, the invariant of that subgroup. Three predictions follow. Fitting the transformation between a healthy and a collapsed representation and applying it to the healthy readout recovers the collapsed model if the drift is a change of basis. Removing hidden weight decay triples a net motion that is the residual of two opposing terms and brings the collapse forward. A decoder fit from scratch on a circuit-failure representation recovers the task if the information survives and only the readout lost access. For interpretability practice the conclusion is immediate: a circuit can be present, correct, and outvoted, and the instruments that certify the first two say nothing about the third. Audits of grokked circuits need a functional measure alongside the spectral ones.
+The tests establish surviving task information, with training-only decoders reaching $98.20$--$100\%$, while rejecting exact global basis equivalence for the measured pairs. Arithmetic corrections suppress joint failures over fixed horizons; captured updates overshoot accurate local descent directions. Together with adjacent swaps and the feature-mean intervention, these results support a numerical contribution to acute readout failure. The relative contributions of feature growth and optimizer history remain unresolved.
+
+The accurate-loss RMS embedding failure limits this account. The main controls cover five selected trajectories; the operation and normalization extensions use one seed each. Behavior beyond $100{,}000$ steps and brief test-only excursions remain unresolved, and AdamW collapses limit attribution specifically to Muon. Full-family Fourier filtering supplies answer-orbit structure and mixes training and test inputs. The memorizer control rules out using perfect filtered accuracy alone as evidence of an arithmetic algorithm.
+
